# The build COPYs only its real inputs (api, cmd, internal, ansible, scripts,
# go.mod/go.sum, Makefile, and .git for version stamping). Everything below is
# excluded from the build context so it neither slows the context transfer nor
# invalidates any build layer. .git is deliberately NOT excluded: a raw
# `docker build` self-stamps version metadata from it in the compile stage, and
# a repo guard test (TestContainerfileStampsBuildMetadata) enforces its presence.
.github/
.agents/
docs/
examples/
specs/
images/
test/
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
mkdocs.yml
.editorconfig
.cache/
.state/
.codex/
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/
auth/
secrets/
bin/
dist/
build/
out/
rendered/
site/
tmp/
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*kubeconfig*
*pull-secret*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
